title: March 2025

@asylum_suspension_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — The roll call now places the live government's security case, the President, border personnel and refugee safeguards against Lewica's recorded doctrine, with a distinct cost on every vote.
title: Parliament authorises temporary asylum suspension
subtitle: Most of the Sejm moves right; much of the Left votes no
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 10
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/events/belarus-border-2021.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 3 and pm_political_family != "left"
on-arrival: {!
const carriedBorderPressure =
    (Number(Q.border_permission_pressure) || 0) +
    Math.max(
        0,
        45 - (Number(Q.border_rights_standard) || 0)
    ) * 0.5 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        8 - (Number(Q.refugee_service_capacity) || 0)
    ) * 1.5;
Q.border_permission_pressure = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(carriedBorderPressure))
);
Q.border_security_confidence += 3;
Q.refugee_empathy -= 5;
Q.democratic_rightward_pressure += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_border_security_support += 14;
Q.public_mood_pending_border_security_salience += 16;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -12;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 12;
Q.news_headline =
    "The border law turns cabinet dissent into a recorded roll call";
!}

= March 2025 — Where does Lewica draw the border line?

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** asks the Sejm for authority to suspend
asylum applications temporarily at the Belarusian border; President **[+
president_name +]** will decide whether the bill becomes law. The government
argues that Minsk is turning applicants into instruments of pressure. Refugee
lawyers, medics and families seeking protection ask who remains able to reach a
procedure when the gate is closed.

Lewica enters the roll call with **[+ border_doctrine +]** as its operational
record and **[+ asylum_position_2025 +]** as its coalition promise. Border
guards want rules they can apply; Razem and much of our own movement expect a
rights line that survives office. We may reverse ourselves, but nobody in the
chamber will mistake the reversal for continuity.

- @asylum_vote_no
- @asylum_safeguards
- @asylum_support

@asylum_vote_no
title: Vote no and accept the parliamentary consequences
subtitle: Keep the rights doctrine intact and open a breach with the governing majority.
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Voted against asylum suspension"; border_rights_standard += 5; progressive_credibility += 4; ko_relation -= 5 if government_party = "ko"; pis_relation -= 5 if government_party = "pis"; psl_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 5 if left_in_government = 1; razem_cooperation += 4; public_trust -= 2; border_permission_pressure -= 4; news_headline = "Lewica records a principled vote against suspension"

Lewica's deputies vote no beside Razem and a small rights minority. Lawyers and
humanitarian groups receive an opposition they can quote in court; coalition
whips receive proof that our border doctrine has a limit. Security-minded
voters hear dissent while the government is asking for unity.

- @poland_event_queue: Record Lewica's no vote

@asylum_safeguards
title: Abstain after securing medical, child and court-review exceptions
subtitle: Narrow the suspension without endorsing it; refugee organisers will still record a retreat.
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Abstained after enforceable exceptions"; border_rights_standard += 3; constitutional_restraint += 3; ko_relation += 2; psl_relation += 1; progressives_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; border_permission_pressure += 1; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 6; public_mood_pending_border_security_support += 3; news_headline = "Humanitarian exceptions narrow the suspension"

Medical emergencies, children and access to judicial review are written into
the bill before Lewica abstains. Border services gain a narrower rule and the
coalition keeps enough votes. Refugee organisations acknowledge the openings
without calling a suspension humane merely because it has exceptions.

- @poland_event_queue: File the safeguarded abstention

@asylum_support
title: Support the government line as a response to Belarus
subtitle: Join the security consensus at the cost of owning the suspension before refugee advocates.
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Supported temporary asylum suspension"; border_doctrine = "Security consensus and asylum suspension"; border_security_confidence += 5; military_trust += 2; ko_relation += 4 if government_party = "ko"; pis_relation += 4 if government_party = "pis"; psl_relation += 3; refugee_empathy -= 6; minority_safety -= 4; razem_cooperation -= 6; far_right_agenda += 3; border_permission_pressure += 8; news_headline = "Lewica backs the government's asylum-suspension line"

Lewica votes with the security majority and lets the government call the bill
a national answer to Belarus. Relations with the governing camp warm and
officers receive a clear political instruction. Razem, refugee advocates and
minority organisers now treat the suspension as part of our record, not a
measure imposed despite us.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the security vote

@gender_recognition_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — The Supreme Court ruling is experienced through trans applicants, their parents, registrars and Kotula's equality campaign; administrative action now requires Lewica's justice or digital portfolio, and even then judicial guidance remains non-binding.
title: The Supreme Court simplifies gender recognition
subtitle: Everyday legal procedure advances without a parliamentary majority
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 11
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/cards/equality-bill.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 3
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 2; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 11; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 5; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 7; news_headline = "Trans people no longer need to sue their parents under the new Supreme Court route"

= March 2025 — Defend the ruling or legislate the right

The Civil Chamber of the Supreme Court has ended the fiction that a trans
person must sue their parents to correct the sex marker on a civil record.
Applicants and their families can now use a non-contentious procedure, but
registrars and lower courts still need to know what a consistent practice looks
like.

Lewica's equality campaign, led in parliament by <span class="party-lewica"><b>Katarzyna Kotula</b></span>, can turn
the judgment into a statutory right. A Lewica justice or digital minister can
also make the procedure easier to use within that office's authority, but no
minister may instruct an independent court how to decide a case. Without either
portfolio, the party is limited to legislation, coalition pressure and legal
support. Silence avoids a culture-war launch only by leaving the people who won
the case to police its implementation.

- @gender_statute
- @gender_guidance
- @gender_opposition_toolkit
- @gender_quiet

@gender_statute
title: Introduce a full self-determination and recognition statute
subtitle: Turn procedural relief into a uniform right and open a fight with PSL and the Palace.
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 6; minority_safety += 5; psl_relation -= 7; president_relation -= 5; far_right_agenda += 5; government_coalition_dissent += 5; news_headline = "The Left turns a procedural ruling into a national rights bill"

Kotula introduces a self-determination statute that replaces procedural mercy
with a uniform right. Trans organisations gain a bill around which to organise;
PSL and the Palace prepare to oppose its scope. The judgment is protected
politically, but no statute has yet passed.

- @poland_event_queue: File the national recognition bill

@gender_guidance
title: [? if digital_minister_party = "Lewica": Standardise registry forms and request judicial guidance?][? if digital_minister_party != "Lewica" and justice_minister_party = "Lewica": Fund judicial guidance and press the registry ministry to follow it?]
subtitle: Use the portfolio Lewica actually holds; courts receive model practice from judicial bodies, never a ministerial instruction.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and (digital_minister_party = "Lewica" or justice_minister_party = "Lewica")
on-arrival: minority_safety += 4; court_user_trust += 3; government_delivery += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; progressives_dissent += 1; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 6; news_headline = "Administrative guidance makes the judgment usable"

[? if digital_minister_party = "Lewica": Digital Affairs sends civil
registries standard forms and data-handling instructions within its own remit.
The ministry asks the Supreme Court and judicial training bodies to publish
model practice for judges; it does not order a court to reach a result.?]
[? if digital_minister_party != "Lewica" and justice_minister_party = "Lewica":
The Justice Ministry funds training and circulates the Supreme Court's ruling,
then asks the competent judicial bodies for model practice. It presses the
cabinet owner of the civil register to standardise forms, but cannot sign that
office's instruction in its place.?] Applicants gain a route that is easier to
use. Activists welcome the work while reminding Lewica that guidance can be
withdrawn more easily than a right enacted in law.

- @poland_event_queue: File the registry guidance

@gender_opposition_toolkit
title: [? if left_in_government = 1 and caretaker_government = 0: Publish a legal toolkit and force the responsible coalition ministers to answer?][? if left_in_government = 0 or caretaker_government = 1: Publish a legal toolkit and fund test cases against inconsistent practice?]
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Make obstruction contestable without claiming authority the party does not hold.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 or caretaker_government = 1 or (digital_minister_party != "Lewica" and justice_minister_party != "Lewica")
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The caucus cannot staff the legal network.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; minority_safety += 3; court_user_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; media_capacity += 1; progressive_credibility += 2; news_headline = "Opposition lawyers publish a model procedure and challenge registries case by case"

Lewica funds model applications, a registry manual and counsel for the first
inconsistent refusals. The network cannot command national administration or
the courts.[? if left_in_government = 1 and caretaker_government = 0: Our
coalition partners who hold Justice and Digital Affairs must now defend every
gap between the judgment and their practice.?][? if left_in_government = 0 or
caretaker_government = 1: It can still make a local official's obstruction
expensive and visible while the party builds the case for legislation.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Send the legal toolkit to the events desk

@gender_quiet
title: Let the ruling work without opening a campaign front
subtitle: Avoid an immediate backlash and leave applicants to enforce the victory case by case.
on-arrival: court_user_trust += 1; progressive_credibility -= 2; minority_safety += 1; far_right_agenda -= 1; news_headline = "A quiet procedural gain avoids immediate parliamentary reversal"

The party issues no national challenge and lets lawyers circulate the ruling
quietly. Some applicants benefit before the right builds a campaign against
the change. Others still meet a doubtful court or registry alone, and equality
organisers learn that Lewica preferred a low profile to ownership.

- @poland_event_queue: Let the quiet ruling enter the record

@movement_spring_audit_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — Women's Strike organisers, legal-clinical networks and Lewica's equality figures now audit a specific promise, while every settlement ends in a visible political verdict.
title: The abortion-rights promise comes due
subtitle: The post-defeat settlement is tested against a cabinet calendar
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 23
order: 12
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/events/womens-strike-2020.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 3 and movement_reckoning_2024_done = 1 and abortion_reform_settled = 0
on-arrival: public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 9; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_left_ownership += -6; news_headline = "The reproductive-rights movement audits the Left's post-defeat promise"

= March 2025 — Organisers ask what was delivered

Women's Strike organisers, abortion-support networks, clinicians and lawyers
return with the promise Lewica made after the previous defeat. **Katarzyna
Kotula** and **Magdalena Biejat** can no longer answer them with another rally:
the audit concerns a vote, access, candidates or an admitted breach.

[? if abortion_law_enacted: After the July bill became law, the party offered
**[+ movement_reckoning_result +]**. The audit now concerns access and movement
power, not another unnecessary passage vote.?]
[? if not abortion_law_enacted: After the July bill was blocked, the party
offered **[+ movement_reckoning_result +]**.?]
[? if abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1: The promised spring vote is now due. A
presidential campaign is not an extension of the deadline.?]
[? if movement_candidates_promised = 1: Organisers can name the districts,
selection meetings and safe places where the candidate promise either exists
or does not.?]
[? if movement_reckoning_result = "Clinical access and legal defence before another vote":
Lawyers and clinicians bring casework rather than a rally attendance figure.
They want to know which ministry will keep the network operating.?]
[? if movement_reckoning_result = "Party command of the reproductive-rights campaign":
The party controls the mailing list and stage. It does not control whether
former organisers believe its account of the defeat.?]

- @movement_spring_vote
- @movement_spring_access
- @movement_spring_candidates
- @movement_spring_breach

@movement_spring_vote
title: Put the promised vote on the calendar and make PSL answer in public
subtitle: Available only if the cabinet deadline was promised.
view-if: abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1 and abortion_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: movement_followthrough_2025 = "The promised vote was tabled"; abortion_cabinet_deadline = 0; feminist_trust += 6; progressive_credibility += 3; psl_relation -= 8; government_coalition_dissent += 7; early_election_risk += 4; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The spring abortion vote reaches the Sejm calendar"
go-to: movement_spring_roll_call

@movement_spring_roll_call
title: The promised roll call
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.abortion_rewrite_pending) {
    Q.abortion_implementation_prepared = 1;
    Q.abortion_rewrite_pending = 0;
}
Q.abortion_spring_local_bonus = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        11,
        Math.round(
            ((Number(Q.local_network) || 0) - 30) / 4
        )
    )
);
Q.abortion_spring_movement_bonus = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        8,
        Math.round(
            ((Number(Q.movement_leverage) || 0) - 45) / 6
        )
    )
);
Q.legvote_bill_name = "The spring abortion-decriminalisation bill";
Q.legvote_profile = "abortion";
Q.legvote_callback = "movement_spring";
Q.legvote_president_commitment = 0;
Q.legvote_campaign_bonus =
    Q.abortion_spring_local_bonus + Q.abortion_spring_movement_bonus;
Q.legvote_palace_bonus = 25 +
    (Q.abortion_implementation_prepared ? 8 : 0) +
    (Q.abortion_strategy == "Decriminalisation sequence" ? 5 : 0) +
    (Q.abortion_strategy == "Material compromise" ? 4 : 0);
Q.legvote_prepared = 0;
Q.legvote_enacted = 0;
Q.legvote_effects_applied = 0;
!}
go-to: poland_legislative_vote

@movement_spring_return
go-to: poland_events_2024_07.abortion_presidential_decision if abortion_spring_passed = 1; poland_event_queue if abortion_spring_passed = 0

@movement_spring_vote_result
title: The movement records the whole legislative route
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.legvote_effects_applied) {
    Q.abortion_spring_yes = Number(Q.legvote_sejm_yes) || 0;
    Q.abortion_spring_no = Number(Q.legvote_sejm_no) || 0;
    Q.abortion_spring_abstain = Number(Q.legvote_sejm_abstain) || 0;
    Q.abortion_spring_absent = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460) -
            Q.abortion_spring_yes - Q.abortion_spring_no -
            Q.abortion_spring_abstain
    );
    Q.abortion_spring_present =
        Q.abortion_spring_yes + Q.abortion_spring_no +
        Q.abortion_spring_abstain;
    Q.abortion_spring_threshold = Q.abortion_spring_no + 1;
    Q.abortion_spring_passed = Q.legvote_sejm_passed ? 1 : 0;
    if (Q.abortion_spring_passed) {
        if (Q.left_in_government) Q.government_delivery += 7;
        else Q.media_capacity += 3;
        Q.feminist_trust += 8;
        Q.progressive_credibility += 5;
        Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 5;
    } else {
        Q.feminist_trust -= 3;
        Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
        Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
    }
    Q.abortion_law_enacted = Q.legvote_enacted ? 1 : 0;
    Q.abortion_presidential_action = Q.legvote_veto_overridden
        ? "Veto overridden by the Sejm"
        : (Q.legvote_president_veto
            ? "Presidential veto"
            : (Q.legvote_enacted ? "Signed into law" : "No presidential decision"));
    Q.movement_followthrough_2025 = Q.legvote_enacted
        ? "The promised spring abortion bill became law"
        : Q.legvote_outcome;
    Q.last_policy_stage = Q.legvote_enacted
        ? "Enacted ordinary statute"
        : "Failed ordinary statute";
    Q.last_policy_authority = Q.legvote_veto_overridden
        ? "Three-fifths Sejm veto override"
        : (Q.legvote_enacted ? Q.president_name : "Sejm and Senate");
    Q.last_policy_implementation = Q.legvote_enacted
        ? "Enacted; clinical delivery remains to be funded"
        : 0;
    Q.news_headline = Q.legvote_outcome;
    Q.legvote_effects_applied = 1;
}
!}

The movement can now distinguish the forecast, the bargain, the Sejm division,
the Senate response and the presidential decision. **[+ legvote_outcome +].**

- @poland_events_2024_07.abort_pass_implement
- @poland_events_2024_07.abort_signed_monitor
- @poland_events_2024_07.abort_veto_campaign
- @poland_events_2024_07.abort_veto_rewrite
- @poland_event_queue: File the complete division record

